          "type": "hero",
          "id": "s-hero",
          "variant": "pattern",
          "title": "How to Mail Cloth",
          "subtitle": "Sample text — replace me: Size, stiffness, stamps, and what happens when a card comes back crumpled.",
          "style": {
            "bg": "none",
            "align": "center"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "feature_grid",
          "id": "m-grid",
          "variant": "cards",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "Size",
              "body": "4 by 6 inches. Corners may be round. A hanging sleeve is how you get it returned as a parcel."
            },
            {
              "title": "Middle",
              "body": "Cardstock or a thin plastic. Quilted cloth alone will crumple in the machine."
            },
            {
              "title": "Address",
              "body": "Ink on a fabric label, or a paper label stitched on. Pencil disappears."
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "bg": "tint",
            "width": "wide",
            "divider": "scallop",
            "motion": "piece_in"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "faq",
          "id": "m-faq",
          "items": [
            {
              "q": "Do you insure them?",
              "a": "No. That is the point of a postcard. If it vanishes, sew another."
            },
            {
              "q": "International?",
              "a": "A few of us do. Extra stamps, extra time, a customs form that confuses everyone."
            }
          ],
          "style": {
            "bg": "none",
            "width": "narrow",
            "layout": "framed",
            "motion": "piece_in"
          }
